ume


update the architecture+design+requirements+specification docs for the ume platform, integrating in:

the ume platform deploys distributable+deployable+configurable+release operating systems for organizations+businesses, termed "OrgOS", that have configurable/plug-and-play modules that can be flavored/tailored to a specific organizations needs. The ume platform itself is an operating system that serves as a factory for producing tailored operating systems for any organization/business/business-solution. The ume platform provides the baseline infrastructure+kernel for running "orgAps" organization applications, where these applications manage/run an organization (an organization runtime). "Organization Runtimes" realize "organization outcomes", goals, objectives, milestones, tranformations, and so on... An organization effectiviely becomes a series of interconnected running OrgApps all specified, configured, maintained, managed and defined under an OrgSystem, create SDOs software defined organizations, which act as "digital twins" of a physical organization/business. Users operate and interact with SDOs, at the digital twin layer. OrgExec(utors) and OrgCPUs are the running components that take action and execute OrgSystem commands/tasks, with OrgExecs being humans+AI+agents+hybrid systems+custom physical agents and OrgCPUs being digital-agents+machines+devices+3rd party platforms/tools+IoT devices/sensors+, where common interfaces for OrgCPU/OrgExec to OrgKernel/OrgSystem are defined through ODDs organization device drivers, OrgDeviceDrivers. ODDs orgDeviceDrivers are effectively contracts for how an OrgDevice, an entity which executes work on the system, will carry out tasks on and use the OrgOS, so that other system components+devices can plan accordingly and use these devices as necessary, all through a common, agreed upon operating standard/contract. 

For example, when a new user has an idea and wants to start a new business, they will create an account and bootstrap+configure+design their initial organization+organization-operating-system on the ume platform. The user, any employees/contractors, AI assistants and agents would become OrgExecs, executing tasks for the OrgSystem (the business), where contracts+skills+labor-specification are specified through ODD orgDeviceDrivers. The Ume platform offers a configurable business solution that can scale to any organizatoin size, from single entrepreneur to massive enterprise, while maintaining a common set of standards and best practices. Business+Organizations can be effectively "simulated" through their digital twins (OrgSystems+OrgOSs+OrgKernels) and this allows them to be optimized, better maintained, have single source of ground truths, have master data management (OrgDNA) which can be replicated and transmitted to other orgnaizations, allowing for further optimzation and scaling. 

distributed ledger systems DLTs can exist between/among organizations+organization-operating-systems, where contracts (smart contracts) can be executed on these ledger. DLTs are a representation of OrgMemroy, and the memroy between/among a group of organizations, where resources/data/assets are transfered between/among organizations, as defined and specified by smart contracts between+among organizations. Organizations can connect with one another and scale+compose, forming decentralized autonomous organizations, DAOs, effectively making DAOs a set of interconnected+decentralized+distributed organizaitons, that work in tandem/concert together as one, single organization, facilitating vertical and horizontal organization scaling+growth+composability.
